  "term": "social skills training",
  "definition": "Social skills training is a structured method for helping people develop more appropriate and effective social interaction skills. It is traditionally delivered by human trainers, but it can also be provided through computer-based interactive systems that practice both spoken and nonverbal aspects of communication.",
